# ⚠ THIS FILE IS MAINTAINED BY HAND, and deliberately. Tools/publish-public.py mirrors the
# private repository's tree but NOT this file - it ignores itself, on the line below - so
# that the public snapshot can carry its own rules. Every publish prints the rules the
# private .gitignore has and this one lacks, and says "add them by hand if they matter
# here". The block at the bottom is the answer to that prompt.
Memory/
.gitignore
CLAUDE.local.md*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ⛔ EVERYTHING BELOW IS WRITTEN BY THE INSTALLER INTO ITS OWN CLONE, and without these
# rules the clone is DIRTY the moment a full install finishes. Measured on a test VM,
# 2026-10-14: after one complete run, `git status` in C:\WorkSpace\dev-workstation showed
#     M .gitignore        <- Tools/deploy.py appending the two rules below
#     ?? .gitnexus/       <- the GitNexus index
#     ?? CLAUDE.md        <- the project template deploy.py places
#     ?? Debug/           <- install.ps1's OWN run logs
# and install.ps1's self-update then refused to run, correctly, because the tree was not
# clean. So the one-line command updated a machine once and never again - the promise
# degrading silently, which is the failure this project spends most of its comments on.
#
# The modified `.gitignore` was the only TRACKED change, and it was this file's own fault:
# deploy.py appends the manifest rules because they were not here.

# Written by Tools/deploy.py. Per-run, per-machine: the manifest is this clone's own
# deployment state, and a copy of it on a machine that has nothing installed would lie
# about what is deployed.
/.claude/.deploy-manifest.json
/.claude/deploy-report-*.md

# install.ps1's run transcript. One file per run, named for the moment it started.
/Debug/install-*.log

# The GitNexus index for this clone. Per-machine, rebuilt by `gitnexus analyze`, and large.
/.gitnexus/

# The project CLAUDE.md that Tools/deploy.py places here from the template. It is meant to
# be filled in per machine and per person; it is not part of the published snapshot.
/CLAUDE.md
